Feature: Security — Input Validation and Abuse Prevention # features/security.feature:1

  @dev @prod @security
  Scenario Outline: API response to malicious payloads (SQLi / XSS) — contract gap -- @1.1                                 # features/security.feature:26
    When I send a POST request to "/users" with name "Robert'); DROP TABLE users;--", email "sqli@loanpro.com", and age 30 # steps/user_steps.py:81
    Then the response status code should be 400                                                                            # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain a validation error message                                                        # steps/common_steps.py:116

  @dev @prod @security
  Scenario Outline: API response to malicious payloads (SQLi / XSS) — contract gap -- @1.2                                # features/security.feature:27
    When I send a POST request to "/users" with name "<script>alert("XSS")</script>", email "xss@loanpro.com", and age 30 # steps/user_steps.py:81
    Then the response status code should be 400                                                                           # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain a validation error message                                                       # steps/common_steps.py:116

  @dev @prod @security
  Scenario Outline: API response to malicious payloads (SQLi / XSS) — contract gap -- @1.3                           # features/security.feature:28
    When I send a POST request to "/users" with name "<h1>HTML Injection</h1>", email "html@loanpro.com", and age 30 # steps/user_steps.py:81
    Then the response status code should be 400                                                                      # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain a validation error message                                                  # steps/common_steps.py:116

  @dev @prod @security
  Scenario: API response to a massive payload — contract gap             # features/security.feature:31
    When I send a POST request to "/users" with a name of 500 characters # steps/user_steps.py:139
    Then the response status code should be 400                          # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain a validation error message      # steps/common_steps.py:116

Feature: DELETE /users/{email} — Delete User # features/users_delete.feature:1

  @dev @prod
  Scenario: Delete a user successfully with valid authentication                                  # features/users_delete.feature:8
    Given a user with email "delete@loanpro.com" exists                                           # steps/user_steps.py:34
    When I send a DELETE request to "/users/delete@loanpro.com" with a valid Authentication token # steps/user_steps.py:246
    Then the response status code should be 204                                                   # steps/common_steps.py:26

  @dev @prod @BUG-005
  Scenario: Fail to delete a user without authentication                                        # features/users_delete.feature:18
    Given a user with email "noauth@loanpro.com" exists                                         # steps/user_steps.py:34
    When I send a DELETE request to "/users/noauth@loanpro.com" without an Authentication token # steps/user_steps.py:254
    Then the response status code should be 401                                                 # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain an authentication error message                        # steps/common_steps.py:155

  @dev @prod @BUG-005
  Scenario: Fail to delete a user with invalid authentication token                                       # features/users_delete.feature:25
    Given a user with email "invalidauth@loanpro.com" exists                                              # steps/user_steps.py:34
    When I send a DELETE request to "/users/invalidauth@loanpro.com" with an invalid Authentication token # steps/user_steps.py:262
    Then the response status code should be 401                                                           # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain an authentication error message                                  # steps/common_steps.py:155

  @dev @prod
  Scenario: Fail to delete a non-existent user                                                         # features/users_delete.feature:36
    When I send a DELETE request to "/users/nonexistent@loanpro.com" with a valid Authentication token # steps/user_steps.py:246
    Then the response status code should be 404                                                        # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain a user not found error message                                # steps/common_steps.py:142

Feature: GET /users and GET /users/{email} — List and Retrieve Users # features/users_get.feature:1

  @dev @prod
  Scenario: List empty list of users — validate response is a JSON array  # features/users_get.feature:8
    When I send a GET request to "/users"                                 # steps/user_steps.py:154
    Then the response status code should be 200                           # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should be a JSON array                          # steps/common_steps.py:39

  @dev @prod
  Scenario: List multiple users successfully               # features/users_get.feature:14
    Given 10 users are created in the system               # steps/user_steps.py:65
    When I send a GET request to "/users"                  # steps/user_steps.py:154
    Then the response status code should be 200            # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should be a JSON array           # steps/common_steps.py:39
    And the response body should contain at least 10 users # steps/common_steps.py:48

  @dev @prod
  Scenario: Get an existing user by email                      # features/users_get.feature:26
    Given a user with email "existing@loanpro.com" exists      # steps/user_steps.py:34
    When I send a GET request to "/users/existing@loanpro.com" # steps/user_steps.py:160
    Then the response status code should be 200                # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain the user details      # steps/common_steps.py:69

  @dev @prod @BUG-004
  Scenario: Fail to get a non-existent user                             # features/users_get.feature:33
    When I send a GET request to "/users/nonexistent@loanpro.com"       # steps/user_steps.py:160
    Then the response status code should be 404                         # steps/common_steps.py:26
    And the response body should contain a user not found error message # steps/common_steps.py:142

